WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:02.175
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:03.008
- Hi!
- [Kelly] I know, I love it!

00:00:03.008 --> 00:00:04.626
I had no idea you were
coming on until last night!

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:08.247
- I miss you so much! LA
feels your missing presence.

00:00:08.247 --> 00:00:09.450
- Oh, I just loved it.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.996
Last night, I was in bed
and I was like, "Oh, crap!

00:00:11.996 --> 00:00:13.456
I was like, "I didn't know
Chrissy was coming on today."

00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:15.054
- Honestly, I didn't even
know Dave was gonna be here.

00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:16.330
(all laughing)

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.163
- You were like, "Wait,
what are you doing here?

00:00:17.163 --> 00:00:18.030
"Oh, we're doing a show."

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.350
Now when did y'all first meet?

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.760
You've known each other for years, right?

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.260
Did you bond over food?

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.390
- 2004 when I first opened my restaurant.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.260
- Yeah.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.520
- Oh, here? So you were living here?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.920
- I was living in New York
when I had first met John,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.270
and yeah, I'm 38 now.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.490
We've known each other 20 years.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.890
We always hit up Momofuku Noodle Bar.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:35.730
It was right by our house.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.110
We lived in the East Village,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.700
and we went there three,
four times a week,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.590
and then I just fell in love with him.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.863
- That's right.

00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:42.696
- Great food.

00:00:42.696 --> 00:00:43.529
Well, it's hard not to
fall in love with you,

00:00:43.529 --> 00:00:45.630
especially being he cooks so well.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.250
But where did your love of cooking start?

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.083
I'll start with you, David.

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:48.990
- I think with my mom.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.350
She's just still was the
best cook I've ever met,

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.620
and that was the only way my
family sort of communicated was

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.580
through food.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.023
Never anything else, but.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.181
- There's some therapy in the workings!

00:01:02.181 --> 00:01:03.930
- I think it's like our common
Asian bond, though, too.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.240
I think a lot of, my family at least,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.470
there weren't a lot of, like,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.277
there wasn't a lot of physical affection,

00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:11.040
kisses and I love yous,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.900
but food was so important in our family.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.780
And now, looking back and
having children, I do realize

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.200
that I'm very, I mean, I
smother them with love,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.420
but they also get a ton of great food.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.100
- I know, I think it's
so great when you learn

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.410
at such a young age how to
cook or to be in a kitchen

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.880
and how to, like, that's amazing.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.507
I'm the opposite.

00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:29.340
(Chrissy laughs)

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.297
You know.

00:01:30.297 --> 00:01:33.060
But you have two boys. Do
they help in the kitchen now?

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.700
- Yes, four and two, Hugo and Gus.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.533
- [Kelly] Taste test?

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:39.180
- They tell me what to cook.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.520
They try to help, and
I'm their private chef,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.490
and no matter what I make,
they almost never eat,

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.960
so it's a problem for me.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.850
- That actually makes me feel good,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.860
'cause when I do cook, I'm like,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.203
do you know how hard this was for me?

00:01:53.148 --> 00:01:54.960
I don't do this, and I
feel like I did a good job,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.580
and they do not eat it.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.290
And I'm like, it makes me feel good

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.910
that you're an actual chef.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.047
And yeah, they just are like,

00:02:02.047 --> 00:02:03.890
"Hard pass. Where's the mac and cheese?"

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.723
- Yeah, they want mac and cheese.

00:02:04.723 --> 00:02:06.750
They want all shades of brown foods.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.450
- Beige! My son eats nothing but beige!

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.283
- Beige anything.

00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:11.580
Mine, it's gotten to the point

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.040
where I definitely take orders,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.160
but I have to actually just,
at this point with Miles,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.590
I said it the other day,
he doesn't eat vegetables.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.720
And I mean, like, not a carrot stick.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.553
It's just like a big like fight with him.

00:02:22.553 --> 00:02:24.345
- My son! My son will not, yeah.

00:02:24.345 --> 00:02:25.443
- [Chrissy] Thank you!
- He's like, absolutely not.

00:02:25.443 --> 00:02:26.610
- No one wants to admit to that,

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.560
but then I was like, oh
no, it goes past that.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.970
Like, I can offer him a root beer float.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:30.900
Like, he doesn't wanna try that.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.500
He doesn't wanna, I'm like,
"Please try this Coca-Cola."

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.570
And then I'm like, why am
I being, why am I trying?

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.780
It's just, it's crazy.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.850
- No, but my son is the same, though.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:42.270
I have to sneak it in into
a cup that's colorful,

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.100
that you can't tell what the color is.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.270
And that's how I sneak it in.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.150
It's like a juice or a
smoothie. He will not do it.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.827
And he will smell it out and be like,

00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:51.930
"This is a vegetable."

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.880
And he is, like, hard against it. Yeah.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.075
- [Chrissy] Same.

00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:57.120
- I mean, and it's like, I
could make him sit there,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.160
you know, or whatever,
but it just doesn't work.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:02:59.993
He'll sit me out.

00:02:59.993 --> 00:03:00.826
- I know.

00:03:00.826 --> 00:03:02.010
- He will be like, "Of,
I'll sit at this table

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:02.843
all night long."

00:03:02.843 --> 00:03:05.017
- Before kids, you're like,
"If they don't eat what I make,

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:06.270
"then they're going to bed hungry."

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.598
I'm like, nope, no. "What
would you like, sir?"

00:03:08.598 --> 00:03:09.840
(audience laughs)

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.397
- No, I will say if my son were here,

00:03:11.397 --> 00:03:13.120
I'd have sent him to bed hungry.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.250
(all laughing)

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.250
Because usually, I'm tired!
I'm like, I just did this.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.206
If you didn't like it,
that's your problem.

00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:20.039
(Chrissy laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:03:20.039 --> 00:03:23.940
I'm like, "I made exactly what
you said!" and then whatever.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.160
So you now have more family members

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:26.993
since you've been on the show now.

00:03:26.993 --> 00:03:28.805
- So many!
- How's it going?

00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:31.080
- We have two new little
babies. It's crazy, it's wild.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.423
I love, it's chaotic, obviously.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.680
Wren is six, just turned six
months, or sorry, seven months,

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.420
and Esti just turned a year.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:44.420
And that small difference is
huge when they're that tiny.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.310
And Luna and Miles are
just immersed in activities

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.420
and so many different things

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.717
and everybody's at this different stage.

00:03:49.717 --> 00:03:51.390
- To keep up with as
a parent is very hard.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.550
- Oh my God, the Girl Scouts stuff!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.383
We're in cookie season.

00:03:54.383 --> 00:03:56.610
- You want them to be
engaged. That's me, too.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:59.430
But then it's just like, there's no way

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.567
to feasibly make all of these things.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.647
- And I ask them, I say,

00:04:02.647 --> 00:04:04.710
"What is one activity we should remove?"

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.030
And Miles is always like, "Tennis!"

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.920
He doesn't like tennis
'cause it's too one-on-one.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.115
He can't get away with
any of his bull crap.

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:10.948
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:04:10.948 --> 00:04:12.810
And then with Luna, she's like, "Nothing."

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.520
And this one, she does everything.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.680
- That's my daughter. Same thing.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.180
Well, Esti just turned one,

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.000
and there were some photos from
her birthday like this one.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.237
- [Chrissy] Yeah!

00:04:22.237 --> 00:04:23.070
(audience coos)

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.976
You're like, "This one."
That's the only one

00:04:24.976 --> 00:04:29.040
- Y'all make the cutest children
ever. They're so beautiful.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.816
Wait, and then there's
this one. This one's fun.

00:04:31.816 --> 00:04:33.840
(audience laughs and coos)

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.060
It seems expensive. What was broken?

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.010
- It was immediately after,
I honestly don't know

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.660
because that is a rental home.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.240
And so then I realized
that they're probably

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.340
going to see that.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.530
Or they saw it for sure.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.100
But yeah, my reflex time,
I used to just like,

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.310
with Luna, like, oh, I would've
caught that in a second.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.790
This one, I watched it go
boom-da, boom-da, boom-da,

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.900
and then I just let it happen.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.350
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah, that's
having more than one kid.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.370
You're like, it's fine.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.500
- The worst is how proud she was after.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.960
Usually, they cry or something.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.810
She's just, yeah, she's our tough cookie.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.190
- Yeah, I get it. Girls.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.221
Girls and boys, they're so different.

00:05:13.221 --> 00:05:15.755
That was a look at their new
show Chrissy and Dave Dine Out.

00:05:15.755 --> 00:05:18.043
You can see it on Freeform and Hulu.

00:05:18.043 --> 00:05:19.530
So explain the show to everybody.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.790
- Well, Chrissy and I have been wanting

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.470
to do this together for a long time,

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.150
and we wanted to highlight

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.070
some of the best
restaurants in Los Angeles.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:27.000
- There's so many good ones.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.050
- So many.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.880
And have great conversations

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.640
with very interesting, amazing people.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.866
- Do you know what?

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:36.150
I was actually, I was
coming from a place of like,

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:37.710
there's nowhere good to eat anymore.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.680
And then this guy comes up
with this incredible list,

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.420
and then it opened up my eyes, my palate,

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.890
my everything to different worlds.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:47.310
Some of the chefs that
we got to eat, dine with,

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.770
and speak to completely changed my life,

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:50.910
completely changed my outlook.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.820
I mean, I'm sure you know,
when it comes to work and food,

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.960
when it becomes like your
work, the passion can dull out

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:01.140
when you have four kids,
but it reignited my fire

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.610
for incredible food.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.130
- Yeah, and I think
that's good timing as well

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.670
just 'cause I think the industry
was hit so hard with COVID.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.650
All those restaurants. So many closed.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.330
So to highlight them
is incredible as well.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.230
- Yeah, we actually have
restaurants that are reopening now

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.459
because of the show, so.

00:06:17.459 --> 00:06:19.524
- Oh, that's amazing! I
didn't even even know that.

00:06:19.524 --> 00:06:20.940
That's crazy. But they
were hit really hard.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.820
Like a lot of great places
went out. But how did you pick?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.520
- There was an initial list of like 100,

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:30.090
and I don't think we could
have ever have done it justice,

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.920
so hopefully there's more seasons

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.960
so we can cover all
the awesome restaurants

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.091
that we love so much.

00:06:35.091 --> 00:06:35.924
- Just put it on. You
don't have to watch it.

00:06:35.924 --> 00:06:38.790
Just put it on the
television and just let it-

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:39.840
- Just get those ratings up.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.090
- I'm like, I don't even
know how Nielsen works,

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.710
but I assume you're all Nielsen families.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.390
- I do, too. I don't know
how they work, either.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.537
Every time someone says
rating, I'm like, what?

00:06:46.537 --> 00:06:48.330
I'm like, I dunno.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.540
Anyway, you had the greatest exit at a job

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.860
that I've heard of.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.040
So before becoming a chef, you
worked, like, an office job.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:56.873
- I did.

00:06:56.873 --> 00:06:58.530
- And how did this end, David?

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:01.320
- Well, I wanted to make
sure that I was gonna burn

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.456
all the bridges so I couldn't go back.

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:04.290
(audience laughs)

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.546
- Well done.

00:07:05.546 --> 00:07:06.379
- And I'm gonna say,

00:07:06.379 --> 00:07:08.160
I told everyone I was
gonna go to cooking school

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.660
so I had no choice,

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.380
but I got really drunk
at a Christmas party.

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.213
- [Chrissy] That'll do it.

00:07:14.213 --> 00:07:16.530
- I told a lot of people
how I thought about the job,

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.600
and yeah.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.490
- And amazingly enough,
they didn't ask you back.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:22.463
- Yep, not a surprise.

00:07:22.463 --> 00:07:23.580
- I know, but I feel like a lot of people,

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.837
I've heard people exiting jobs like this,

00:07:24.837 --> 00:07:27.120
but I'm like, "That's such a goal!"

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.650
- I mean, very few people are inspired

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.589
by the movie Office Space,
but I certainly was.

00:07:30.589 --> 00:07:31.422
- Oh my God, I love Office Space.

00:07:31.422 --> 00:07:34.200
- Oh my gosh, yes! Fax
machine out the window, done.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.150
- Or that traffic scene
in the very beginning.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.550
It's so true. You get to
the lane and it stops.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:39.932
Why?
- I know!

00:07:39.932 --> 00:07:41.820
(indistinct) every time.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.920
- Oh God, what a great movie.
Well, I have to say this, too.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.050
John's birthday was last month.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.603
John's greatest gift is you,

00:07:48.603 --> 00:07:49.436
because I'm telling you what,

00:07:49.436 --> 00:07:51.450
this party, first of all, was insane.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.860
- Feel free to text him that.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:56.670
- No, and then also, your gift.
We couldn't air your gift.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.908
This is daytime TV, but I saw one of them-

00:07:58.908 --> 00:08:01.454
(audience screams)

00:08:01.454 --> 00:08:02.576
- [Chrissy] Oh my God!

00:08:02.576 --> 00:08:04.767
(Chrissy screams indistinctly)

00:08:04.767 --> 00:08:05.845
(audience claps)

00:08:05.845 --> 00:08:07.250
- [Kelly] It's a big screen.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.230
- If you know me, too,
I am not a performer.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:11.640
- You're not.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.590
You seem like you'd be like this person,

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:14.880
but you're not, like behind the scenes,

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.890
like you're actually more reserved,

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.803
so to see you give a lap
dance in front of people.

00:08:18.803 --> 00:08:21.660
- They let me come the
night before for rehearsal,

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:22.890
and they're like, "Rehearsal?"

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.540
Like, "It's just a lap dance."

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.470
Like, "What are you thinking?"

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:27.930
And I was like, "No,
no, I need a rehearsal."

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.740
And we did it and having
to lie to John was so crazy

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.140
'cause and just the-

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:37.020
- Who was the rehearsal man for that?

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.103
- My stylist Alana.

00:08:39.286 --> 00:08:41.573
So she was, I had to lick her face.

00:08:41.573 --> 00:08:44.880
We did top to bottom rehearsal.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:45.870
- Oh my God!

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.460
- And then I had 48 hours to plan it

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.920
because I didn't, it was
Christmas and I didn't realize.

